# Pacman packages for an Arch Linux machine, one package name per line.
# Lines starting with '#' are comments; blank lines are ignored.
#
# hubbabubba reads this file from the cloned myconf during
# `install.py --tags dev` and installs every name with `pacman --needed`.
# That means: adding a package here and pushing is enough to get it on the
# server. Removing one does NOT uninstall it (it may be a dependency of
# something else) — remove it on the server by hand if it truly bothers you.
#
# This list is deliberately a dev-workstation list: shell, editor, tmux, and
# what AstroNvim needs at runtime. No fonts or terminal emulator — the
# laptop terminal renders those. Mason installs its own language servers
# (lua_ls, clangd) at runtime; they are not pacman packages.

fish
tmux

# AstroNvim runtime
neovim
git
ripgrep
fzf
gcc
make
nodejs
tree-sitter

# Fonts
nerd-fonts-cascadia-code
